module Core

### The IEEE-754 classification of a floating-point value, as returned by the
### `fpclassify` method on every floating-point type. Mirrors C `<math.h>`'s
### `FP_NAN` / `FP_INFINITE` / `FP_ZERO` / `FP_SUBNORMAL` / `FP_NORMAL`, with the
### same numeric codes (0..4) so it interoperates with C and can be matched with
### `when`.
choice FpClass
  ### Not-a-number (quiet or signaling).
  NAN: 0
  ### Positive or negative infinity.
  INFINITE: 1
  ### Positive or negative zero.
  ZERO: 2
  ### A subnormal (denormalized) nonzero value.
  SUBNORMAL: 3
  ### A finite, normal (non-subnormal, nonzero) value.
  NORMAL: 4
